xilinx_timer: clearing ENT stops the counter; TINT is write-1-to-clear

QEMU only looked at TCSR.ENT to start a counter. Writing ENT=0 left the
ptimer running, and every TCSR write cleared TINT whatever its bit said.

VEXos MainLoop hits this at boot: XTmrCtr_SelfTest (0x010776C8) loads 0,
sets ENT, waits for the count to move, then writes ENT=0. The counter kept
running, sysTimerSetup then set ENIT|ARHT and the 1 s reload, and ~43 s
later AXI timer 0 started interrupting (INTC0 source 26) once a second for
good, so the callback at 0x01034070 printed "tmr1 0, cntr N" forever. On
hardware the timer stays stopped unless debug command 5 starts it
("StartTimer 0").

Now ENT only starts the counter on a 0->1 edge (as in hardware, setting it
again does not reload), ENT=0 stops it, and writing TINT=0 keeps TINT.

diff --git a/hw/timer/xilinx_timer.c b/hw/timer/xilinx_timer.c
--- a/hw/timer/xilinx_timer.c
+++ b/hw/timer/xilinx_timer.c
@@ -169,17 +169,26 @@
     addr &= 3;
     switch (addr) 
     {
-        case R_TCSR:
+        case R_TCSR: {
+            uint32_t old = xt->regs[R_TCSR];
+
+            /* TINT is write-1-to-clear; writing 0 leaves it set.  */
             if (value & TCSR_TINT)
                 value &= ~TCSR_TINT;
+            else
+                value |= old & TCSR_TINT;
 
             xt->regs[addr] = value & 0x7ff;
-            if (value & TCSR_ENT) {
-                ptimer_transaction_begin(xt->ptimer);
+            /* Start on a 0->1 ENT edge; clearing ENT stops the counter.  */
+            ptimer_transaction_begin(xt->ptimer);
+            if ((value & TCSR_ENT) && !(old & TCSR_ENT)) {
                 timer_enable(xt);
-                ptimer_transaction_commit(xt->ptimer);
+            } else if (!(value & TCSR_ENT)) {
+                ptimer_stop(xt->ptimer);
             }
+            ptimer_transaction_commit(xt->ptimer);
             break;
+        }
  
         default:
             if (addr < ARRAY_SIZE(xt->regs))
